# A chain whose free leaves one pending child per level, alternating two release functions (review P1 of Reussir's
# shared drop stack). Reussir links a deferred record whose release function differs from the one before it through
# its header (entry 23, patches 23-n to 23-p, base l2r-base10): here every one, the functions alternating, so the
# pending children take no stack memory, as natively: at 500000 pairs (10^6 levels)
# peak 45.7 MB against native's 55.2 MB, allocations and bytes as native's, under both integer representations
# (with a 24-byte entry per pending child, l2r-base9-shared: 88.6 MB, bytes 2.26 times native's growth).
125000 | 500000 | 1 2000 | rss 1 4000
